 "split": "screen_long",
 "sentences": [
  "Mentoring interns is one of my priorities, so don't hesitate to reach out if you have any questions or concerns.",
  "Instead, focus on writing clean, tested code, and we'll handle quality assurance at the pull request stage.",
  "Pre-commit hooks can introduce bottlenecks and inconsistencies across different developers' machines.",
  "We prefer a streamlined approach where you commit often and utilize pull requests to their full potential.",
  "That way, we can catch issues collectively and provide feedback in a structured manner.",
  "Yes, absolutely.",
  "Small, atomic commits make it easier to track changes and roll back if needed.",
  "And pull requests should be seen as opportunities for discussion and improvement, not just a formality before merging.",
  "We encourage thorough code reviews and constructive feedback within the team.",
  "Don't hesitate to reach out to your teammates for help or clarification.",
  "I'm confident that you'll make valuable contributions during your internship.",
  "Every mentorship relationship should begin with defining clear, achievable objectives.",
  "We can encourage mentees to set goals in various areas, including communication skills, time management, networking, and even personal branding.",
  "As your mentor, I want to ensure you have the tools and knowledge to succeed.",
  "I want you to forget about pre-commit hooks."
 ],
